{"raw": {"https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201218545086_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Assistant Coach, Men's Rowing", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-14\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJob Title:\u00a0 Assistant Coach- Men\u2019s Rowing Department: Athletics Position Reports to (Position Title):\u00a0 Head Coach- Men\u2019s Rowing Effective Date:\u00a0 08/20/2026 \u00a0 Position Class (Exempt or Non-Exempt):\u00a0 Exempt Position Type (Full Time or Part Time):\u00a0 Full-time Is this a Primary or Additional Position:\u00a0 Primary \u00a0 Job Summary Primary responsibilities are to assist the Head Coach in all aspects of Division I program including, but not limited to, coordinating team travel arrangements, game day personnel management, recruiting and other duties as assigned by the Head Coach or Athletic Administration. This position will also assist the Head Coach in organization, administration, and promotion of the program. Candidates must be committed to the academic and athletic success of the student-athletes. Supervisory Responsibilities Graduate Assistants and/ or Interns\u00a0 Duties/Responsibilities Assisting with any or all the following duties as assigned by Head Coach:\u00a0 SCHEDULING\u2013 Responsible for:\u00a0 Assisting with scheduling of all competition RECRUITING\u2013 Responsible for:\u00a0 Compliance with NCAA recruiting rules and completing associated paperwork in a timely manner Arranging financially responsible recruiting trips Initiating arrangements for all official visits Recruiting students who will be an asset to the University and Department of Athletics and graduate in a timely manner\u00a0 FINANCIAL AID\u2013 Responsible for:\u00a0 Understanding NCAA regulations\u00a0 Initiating process for initial and renewal grants\u00a0 Consistently updating team rosters\u00a0 Meeting athletic grant-in-aid budget .\u00a0 BUDGETS\u2013 Responsible for:\u00a0 Assisting in annual budget preparation\u00a0 Staying within amount budgeted for fiscal year\u00a0 Having all expenditures pre-approved through appropriate channels\u00a0 TRAVEL\u2013 Responsible for:\u00a0 Initiating process for all travel arrangements and submitting reports within 48 hours of return\u00a0 EQUIPMENT/APPAREL\u2013 Responsible for:\u00a0 Pre- and Post-season inventory\u00a0 Care and maintenance of all equipment/apparel and facilities Initiating process to order equipment/apparel\u00a0 ACADEMICS\u2013 Responsible for:\u00a0 Supporting all Department of Athletics policies on classroom attendance, study hall, progress reports and enforcing disciplinary actions\u00a0 Working with teams to maintain and increase their\u00a0 APR FUNDRAISING\u2013 Responsible for:\u00a0 Getting prior approval from Advancement prior to initiating a fund raising activity\u00a0 Devising new methods of fund raising\u00a0 Being available for Departmental fund raising activities\u00a0 Following guidelines established by Department, University, and the NCAA for fund raising activities\u00a0 PAPERWORK \u2013 Responsible for:\u00a0 Completing all paperwork by established athletic department and NCAA deadlines\u00a0 MEETINGS \u2013 Responsible for:\u00a0 Attending and contributing to all Department of Athletics meetings and requested functions\u00a0 CAMPS - Responsible for:\u00a0 Following guidelines established by Department, University, and the NCAA for camp procedures and operations Required Skills/Abilities Knowledge of NCAA Rules and Regulations\u00a0 Mastery of sport coached\u00a0 Ability to lead, guide and direct graduate assistants, interns and student-athletes Willingness to form relationships with constituents and help fundraise\u00a0 Education and Experience Minimum Education Requirement:\u00a0 Bachelor\u2019s degree from accredited college or university, master\u2019s degree preferred Minimum Work Experience:\u00a0 Two years collegiate coaching experience at NCAA Division I level preferred 3 Preferred Qualifications:\u00a0 Experience with NCAA Division I Rules and Regulations\u00a0 Proven recruiting abilities\u00a0 Demonstrated leadership skills Physical Requirements Must be able to physically perform essential job duties or have special accommodations arranged in advance\u00a0 Work Conditions:\u00a0 Required to work atypical hours including nights, weekends, potential holidays\u00a0 May be required to practice in heat, cold, inclement weather Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs.\u00a0 To Apply: Please submit your resume with your JU application. Benefits and Perks of Life @ JU All Full Time Positions: Generous paid time off, including vacation, sick leave, jury duty, and bereavement leave\u00a0 Paid Federal Holidays\u00a0 Additional time off for Thanksgiving, Winter holidays, and Spring Break\u00a0 FSA/HSA eligibility\u00a0 Retirement plan with a dollar-for-dollar University match of up to 6% following the vesting period\u00a0 Robust health benefits (medical, dental, vision)\u00a0 100% Employer-Sponsored benefits: Short Term Disability (buy-up option available), Long Term Disability, Employee Assistance Program, Life Insurance, Parent Leave\u00a0 Additional benefit options: Accident coverage, Pet Insurance, Legal, Critical Illness, Dependent Life\u00a0 Tuition benefits for employees, spouses, and dependent children up to 26 years of age\u00a0 Domestic Partner benefit eligibility\u00a0 Veteran and Military Service Support Program\u00a0 Discounted on-campus dining meal plans; 2 free meals per week during Fall and Spring semesters\u00a0 Monthly wellness initiatives\u00a0 Service awards & Recognition programs\u00a0 10% discounts at the on-campus JU Bookstore, School of Orthodontics\u00a0 Free Microsoft Office downloads to personal computers/devices\u00a0 Free on-campus parking\u00a0 Access to campus amenities, including the fitness center, resort-style pool, and library\u00a0 Disclaimer: Benefits and time-off programs are subject to eligibility requirements and may vary based on position and employment status.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201216017705_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Chairside Assistant", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-05\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJob Title: Chairside Assistant - Patient Records Maintenance Department: College of Healthcare Sciences / School of Orthodontics Position Reports to (Position Title): BRCHS Dean / Business Operation Manager Position Class (Exempt or Non-Exempt): Non-Exempt Position Type (Full Time or Part Time): Full Time\u00a0 Is this a Primary or Additional Position: Primary Job Summary Responsible for preparing exam rooms, delivering supplies to service provider, stocking exam rooms, taking x-rays and sterilizing and maintaining instruments. Supervisory Responsibilities None Duties/Responsibilities Prepares patient for treatment, sets up instrument trays, prepares materials, and assists service provider in performing orthodontic procedures. Remove wires for patient to have dental cleaning if doctor is not available. Takes diagnostic x-rays. Instructs patients in oral hygiene and plaque control programs. Makes preliminary impressions for study casts and occlusal registrations for mounting study casts; pours, pulls casts, and returns to resident. Sterilizes and disinfects instruments. Provides postoperative instructions to patients, as prescribed by service provider. Records treatment information in patient records. Takes and records medical and dental histories and\u00a0vital signs of patients if doctor is not available. Tracks lab procedures, ensuring that results are returned within required time frames. Assist Clinical Assistant Coordinator with maintaining supply and material inventories to order replacements as needed. Performs housekeeping tasks to maintain exam and\u00a0treatment rooms and storage areas in a clean, orderly condition. Maintains OSHA requirements and standards. Maintains confidentiality; protects the security of dental records and adheres to all HIPAA guidelines/regulations. Operates standard office equipment and uses required software applications. Sending patient records to doctors\u2019 offices, and patients Back up for maintain appliance tracking system. Communicate low inventory by writing it on the inventory log and write on the maintenance log for maintenance on the dental chairs assigned section. \u00a0 Required Skills/Abilities Knowledge of: Dental terminology. Orthodontic dentistry chair-side assistance processes and procedures. Sterilization techniques and procedures. OSHA standards and requirements. Florida Laws and Regulations Skill in: Providing chair-side assistance. Sterilizing and disinfecting dental equipment Operating and maintaining a wide variety of dental\u00a0equipment. Accurately maintaining patient treatment records. Operating standard office equipment and using required software applications. Ability to: Read understand and follow oral and written instructions. Organize and prioritize multiple detailed tasks within tight timeframes. Communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. Work collaboratively within a team environment. Handle stressful situations and provide a high level of customer service in a calm and professional manner. Inducing calming fearful patients. Establish and maintain effective working relationships with patients, service provider\u2019s faculty and other staff. \u00a0 Education, Certificates, Licenses, and Experience Bachelor's Degree in Business Administration or\u00a0other related discipline two (2) years\u2019 experience in providing secretarial and administrative support to executives in an academic medical environment or an equivalent combination of education, training or experience. A valid driver\u2019s license is required prior to employment and must be maintained during employment. Physical Requirements Sitting up to 7 hours a day Walking up to 3 hours per day Standing up to 7 hours per day Computer keyboard up to 6 hours per day Lifting will not generally apply Pushing will not generally apply Pulling will not generally apply The following requirements will generally not apply:\u00a0 Bending Squatting Stooping Reaching Balancing Twisting Crawling Kneeling Climbing stairs or a ladder Outdoors Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. \u00a0 To Apply Interested candidates are asked to submit a resume, cover letter, and list of references with a JU application.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201208448932_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Chairside Assistant", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-09\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION\u00a0 Job Title: Chairside Assistant - SDS Sheets Maintenance Department: College of Healthcare Sciences / School of Orthodontics Position Reports to (Position Title): BRCHS Dean/Business Operation Manager Position Class (Exempt or Non-Exempt): Non-Exempt Position Type (Full Time or Part Time): Full Time\u00a0 Is this a Primary or Additional Position: Primary Job Summary Responsible for preparing exam rooms, delivering supplies to service provider, stocking exam rooms, taking x rays and sterilizing and maintaining instruments. Supervisory Responsibilities None Duties/Responsibilities Prepares patient for treatment, sets up instrument trays, prepares materials, and assists service provider in performing orthodontic procedures. Remove wires for patient to have dental cleaning if doctor is not available. Takes diagnostic x-rays. Instructs patients in oral hygiene and plaque control programs. Makes preliminary impressions for study casts and occlusal registrations for mounting study casts; pours, pulls casts, and returns to resident. Sterilizes and disinfects instruments. Provides postoperative instructions to patients, as prescribed by service provider. Records treatment information in patient records. Takes and records medical and dental histories and\u00a0vital signs of patients if doctor is not available. Tracks lab procedures, ensuring that results are returned within required time frames. Assist Clinical Assistant Coordinator with maintaining supply and material inventories to order replacements as needed. Performs housekeeping tasks to maintain exam and\u00a0treatment rooms and storage areas in a clean, orderly condition. Maintains OSHA requirements and standards. Maintains confidentiality; protects the security of dental records and adheres to all HIPAA guidelines/regulations. Operates standard office equipment and uses required software applications. Maintain the SDS book (Safety Data Sheets) Maintain appliance tracking system, back up for OSHA Manual maintenance. Communicate low inventory by writing it on the inventory log and write on the maintenance log for maintenance on the dental chairs assigned section. Performs other duties and responsibilities assigned. \u00a0 Required Skills/Abilities Knowledge of: Dental terminology Orthodontic dentistry chair-side assistance processes and procedures. Sterilization techniques and procedures. OSHA standards and requirements. Florida Laws and Regulations. Skill In: Providing chair-side assistance. Sterilizing and disinfecting dental equipment Operating and maintaining a wide variety of dental\u00a0equipment. Accurately maintaining patient treatment records. Operating standard office equipment and using required software applications. Ability to: \u00a0 Read understand and follow oral and written instructions. Organize and prioritize multiple detailed tasks within tight timeframes. Communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. Work collaboratively within a team environment. Handle stressful situations and provide a high level of customer service in a calm and professional manner. Inducing calming fearful patients. Establish and maintain effective working relationships with patients, service provider\u2019s faculty and other staff. \u00a0 Education, Certificates, Licenses, and Experience Bachelor's Degree in Business Administration or other related discipline two (2) years' experience in providing secretarial and administrative support to executives in an academic medical environment or an equivalent combination of education, training or experience.\u00a0 A valid driver's license is required prior to employment and must be maintained during employment. Physical Requirements Sitting\u2014up to 7 hours per day Walking\u2014up to 3 hours per day Standing\u2014up to 7 hours per day Computer keyboard\u2014up to 6 hours per day Lifting will not generally apply Pushing will not generally apply Pulling will not generally apply The following requirements will generally not apply:\u00a0 Bending Squatting Stooping Reaching Balancing Twisting Crawling Kneeling Climbing stairs or a ladder Outdoors Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. \u00a0 To Apply Interested candidates are asked to submit a list of references with the JU Application.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201178504395_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Chairside Assistant", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-09\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION\u00a0 Job Title:\u00a0 Chairside Assistant Department:\u00a0 Brooks College of Healthcare Sciences / School of Orthodontics Position Reports to (Position Title):\u00a0 BRCHS Dean/Business Operation Manager Position Class (Exempt or Non-Exempt): Non-Exempt Position Type (Full Time or Part Time): Full Time Is this a Primary or Additional Position: Primary Job Summary Responsible for preparing exam rooms, delivering supplies to service provider, stocking exam rooms, taking x-rays and sterilizing and maintaining instruments. Duties/Responsibilities Prepares patient for treatment, sets up instrument trays, prepares materials, and assists service provider in performing orthodontic procedures. Remove wires for patient to have dental cleaning if doctor is not available. Takes diagnostic x-rays. Instructs patients in oral hygiene and plaque control programs. Makes preliminary impressions for study casts and occlusal registrations for mounting study casts; pours, pulls casts, and returns to resident. Sterilizes and disinfects instruments. Provides postoperative instructions to patients, as prescribed by service provider. Records treatment information in patient records. Takes and records medical and dental histories and vital signs of patients if doctor is not available. Tracks lab procedures, ensuring that results are returned within required time frames. Assist Clinical Assistant Coordinator with maintaining supply and material inventories to order replacements as needed. Performs housekeeping tasks to maintain exam and treatment rooms and storage areas in a clean, orderly condition. Maintains OSHA requirements and standards. Maintains confidentiality; protects the security of dental records and adheres to all HIPAA guidelines/regulations. Operates standard office equipment and uses required software applications. Sending patient records to doctors\u2019 offices, and patient. Back up for maintain appliance tracking system. Communicate low inventory by writing it on the inventory log and write on the maintenance. L og for maintenance on the dental chairs assigned section. Performance other duties and responsibilities as assigned. Required Skills/Abilities Knowledge of: Dental terminology Orthodontic dentistry chair-side assistance processes and procedures. Sterilization techniques and procedures. OSHA standards and requirements. Florida Laws and Regulations Skill in: Providing chair-side assistance. Sterilizing and disinfecting dental equipment Operating and maintaining a wide variety of dental equipment.\u00a0 Accurately maintaining patient treatment records. Operating standard office equipment and using required software applications. Ability to: Read understand and follow oral and written instructions. Organize and prioritize multiple detailed tasks within tight timeframes. Communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. Work collaboratively within a team environment. Handle stressful situations and provide a high level of customer service in a calm and professional manner. Inducing calming fearful patients. Establish and maintain effective working relationships with patients, service provider\u2019s faculty and other staff. \u00a0 Education and Experience Bachelor's Degree in Business Administration or other related discipline two (2) years\u2019 experience in providing secretarial and administrative support to executives in an academic medical environment or an equivalent combination of education, training or experience. A valid driver\u2019s license is required prior to employment and must be maintained during employment. Physical Requirements Sitting up to 7 hours a day Walking up to 3 hours per day Standing up to 7 hours per day Computer keyboard up to 6 hours per day The following requirements will generally not apply:\u00a0 Bending Lifting Pushing Pulling Squatting Stooping Reaching Balancing Twisting Crawling Kneeling Climbing stairs or a ladder Outdoors Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. \u00a0 To Apply Interested candidates are asked to submit a resume and cover letter with this application.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201208016842_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Clinical Lab Instructor & Simulationist", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-08\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION\u00a0 Job Title:\u00a0 Clinical Lab Instructor & Simulationist Department:\u00a0 Keigwin School of Nursing and Brooks Rehabilitation College of Healthcare Sciences\u00a0 Position Reports to (Position Title):\u00a0 Director of Simulation and Department Chair of Simulation Position Class: Exempt Position Type: Full Time\u00a0 Is this a Primary: Primary \u00a0 Job Description Facilitate the daily operations of the Keigwin School of Nursing (KSON) Simulation Training and Applied Research (STAR) Center and Clinical Skills Lab under the direction of the Simulation Director. The Simulation Center and Clinical Skills Lab are environments that support critical thinking and experiential learning experiences for KSON students, Brooks Rehabilitation College of Healthcare Sciences (BRCHS) students, and community partners. The simulationist/clinical lab instructor will ensure the delivery of clinical simulation experiences, instruction, and the operation of manikin simulators or standardized patients (SPs) to be used effectively in healthcare education and training. Supervisory Responsibilities None Duties/Responsibilities Collaborate with the Department Chair of Simulation and the Director of Simulation, KSON faculty, BRCHS faculty, and community partners to maximize the utilization of clinical learning in simulation centers Collaborate and implement current evidence-based practice in simulation learning set by the International Nursing Association for Clinical Simulation and Learning (INACSL) Lead skill demonstrations, reinforcing classroom theory content in collaboration with faculty Evaluate students' learning and skill acquisition at the discretion of faculty Work with faculty to plan and execute the remediation process to meet assigned course learning objectives. Communicate student outcomes and any related recommendations to faculty Organize and execute the set-up and breakdown of equipment, supplies, and materials for scheduled courses and simulations in the lab and\u00a0classrooms. This includes standardized patient moulage, briefing pre-simulation, debriefing post-simulation, and integrating guided reflection as needed Manage and direct the operation of\u00a0manikin simulators and Standardized Patients (SPs) to facilitate their use in healthcare education and training Facilitate simulation activities that align with course objectives and program outcomes Develop and create ways to enhance learning in the lab, such as facilitating open lab for clinical practice, lunch and learns, and other coordinated activities. Collect and analyze lab survey responses for assigned courses to determine the effectiveness of simulation on student learning, critical thinking, and clinical decision-making. Discuss the findings with the Simulation Director and the faculty course coordinator to identify potential improvements.\u00a0 Provide for the general cleanliness and security of the laboratory. Appropriate disposal of hazardous materials for OSHA standards. Engage and facilitate faculty & community partner development in designing, developing, implementing, and evaluating new courses, simulation scenarios, simulation tools, and other educational initiatives to promote and measure student learning outcomes under the direction of the Simulation Director Communicate and collaborate in a positive, professional manner with faculty, simulationists, and IT operation specialists Collaborate with Simulation Operations and IT specialists to maintain, troubleshoot, and resolve issues related to the operation and maintenance of simulation equipment. Participate in grant and contractual-related activities as designated by the Director of Simulation If certified as an AHA instructor, Train & facilitate the operation of the American Heart Association (AHA) Training Center (or other designated agency) to provide various AHA including but not limited to First Aid,\u00a0BLS (Basic Life Support), PALS (Pediatric Advanced Life Support) & ACLS (Advanced Cardiac Life Support) training for community partners & services. Remain current with developments in the field of simulation technology and learning theory. Participate in professional development and attend professional meetings and conferences Attend regularly scheduled JU KSON meetings and activities as appropriate Participate in simulation meetings for the STAR Center and Skills Lab Participate in KSON organization committee(s) Serve as a mentor and role model for students in the lab Perform other related duties as assigned. Required Skills/Abilities Ability to\u00a0evaluate learners in the teaching/learning simulation lab environment. Knowledge of effective teaching techniques and curriculum development Excellent communication skills (both verbal and written) Technologically inclined and proficient in Microsoft applications Familiar with the healthcare environment and operations, proficient in medical terminology, and well-versed in nursing clinical practices.\u202f Excellent interpersonal and organizational skills Innovative Best Practice simulation curriculum development, implementation, and use of simulation technology. Facilitate the development of learner problem-solving skills Ability to\u00a0work collaboratively with the simulation team, Jacksonville University faculty and staff, and interdisciplinary community partners. May travel between campus buildings or off-campus. Able to work with self-initiative and autonomy. Simulation experience preferred. \u00a0 Education, Certificates, Licenses, and Experience: A Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) from an accredited institution is required. Simulation experience preferred. Medical Surgical, Emergency, Critical Care, Progressive Care Experience Previous teaching experience preferred Unencumbered current Florida nursing license or is eligible to obtain a nursing license in the state of Florida. Current BLS and ACLS certification preferred. AHA Instructor preferred. Certified Healthcare Simulation Educator preferred or a desire to work towards it Physical Requirements Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines. Near vision sufficient to read written communications and computer display screens. Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and by phone. No limitations on physical lifting ability of\u00a0simulation manikins and equipment up to 80 lbs. with assistance No Latex Allergy. Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. To Apply Interested candidates are asked to please submit a JU application, resume, cover letter, and list of references.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9200906362164_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Procurement Specialist", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-06\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJob Description: Procurement Specialist Job Title: Procurement Specialist Reports to: VP of Budget & Procurement Services Department: Procurement Services Position Summary: The Procurement Specialist conducts reviewing and issuing agency purchase orders, administering the University\u2019s vendor file, and assisting in the review and administration of the University\u2019s P-Card program. This role protects the University\u2019s interests by working within established procurement guidelines that ensure best value, while providing quality customer service. The Procurement Specialist will provide procurement guidance to University staff and vendors to ensure all purchases comply with all applicable policies, procedures, and best practices. They will assist in developing complex specifications and scopes of work. \u00a0This position must also develop and maintain effective working relationships with internal and external stakeholders. Key Responsibilities: Purchase Order Administration: Review, process and approve requisitions through the University\u2019s designated purchasing system for the purchase of goods and services. Issue purchase orders Ensure purchase orders and/or purchasing card (PCard) transactions are complete, accurate, and in compliance with all policies, rules, and regulations prior to approving and/or routing for approval. Research and assist departments with information concerning available contracts, prices for needed supplies, equipment and services. Determine proper procurement method and sources of supply. Assist departments to determine correct procurement methods, sources and specifications. Vendor Management: Serve as the primary Vendor Administrator, including obtaining vendor registration applications and required tax forms, creating vendor records in the University\u2019s ERP system, updating records, and inactivating records, as appropriate. Maintain the Procurement Services portion of the JU website to ensure accurate and current information is available to vendors. Represent Procurement Services at various functions, including meetings, tradeshows, and vendor management events PCard Administration Support: Assist the Procurement Analyst in administering the University\u2019s purchasing card program including ordering new cards, managing spend limits and other card controls, and deactivating cards. Assist, when needed, in the review and reconciliation of monthly P-Card statements, providing training to cardholders, reviewing and processing expense reimbursement requests, and identifying discrepancies and potential misuse. Contract Administration Support: Serve as backup to the Procurement Analyst in the management and entry of contractual records in the contract tracking system. Assist the Procurement Analyst, as needed, to facilitate the internal review and approval of contracts and agreements, including liaising with vendors and community partners. Backup Purchasing Support: Serve as the backup for the Procurement Analyst in issuing purchase orders. Serve as the backup for the Procurement Analyst in maintaining the University\u2019s vendor file and supplier contacts. Serve as the backup for the Procurement Analyst in assisting departments in completing and processing purchasing forms. Analysis: Represent Procurement Services in the resolution of contractual problems; determining recourse where possible; preparing correspondence to begin the resolution process; and seeking leadership and legal counsel as needed. Compile information from various sources to prepare reports and ensure that required reports are submitted accurately. Maintain files for purchase orders and other projects as required for auditing purposes; providing auditors with information as requested. Stay abreast of applicable laws, regulations, policies, statutes, and best practices that impact the purchasing/contracting profession. Serve as a liaison between vendors, departments, and Financial Affairs to resolve contractual disputes/problems in a timely manner. Analyze data and make recommendations for improving current processes. Assist leadership staff by bringing unusual problems to their attention, or matters requiring escalation. Qualifications: Education: An associate or bachelor\u2019s degree in business, supply chain management, or a related field is preferred. Equivalent work experience in procurement or a related area will also be considered. Experience: Prior experience in procurement or purchasing roles. Familiarity with purchasing systems, P-Card programs, or ERP software is preferred Skills: Strong organizational abilities, attention to detail, proficiency in procurement software and Microsoft Office Suite, and excellent communication skills. Ability to maintain confidentiality and uphold ethical standards. To Apply Interested candidates are asked to submit a JU application, resume, and list of references.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201197727098_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Director of Enrollment Operations and Analytics", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-01\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJob Title: Director of Enrollment Operations and Analytics \u00a0 Department: Enrollment Management\u00a0 Position Reports to: Vice President, Enrollment Management & Student Success Position Class/Position Type: Exempt \u00a0\u00a0 Job Summary:\u00a0 Reporting to the Vice President of Enrollment Management and Student Success and serving as a core leader within the division, the Director of Enrollment Operations and Analytics provides system leadership, data governance an process optimization to drive strategic enrollment initiatives. This position ensures that admissions operations are efficient, data-informed, compliant, and aligned with institutional enrollment goals. This individual will ensure the high quality leadership to, and execution of technology supported business processes, data management, systems management, project management, and reporting and analytics. This position will be supported by an Admissions Operations Specialist, Graduate Assistant, and student workers. The Director of Enrollment Operations and Analytics will be a thoughtful communicator on issues relevant to recruitment, admissions and financial aid. This individual\u2019s skill in translating complex analyses into clear, actionable insights will benefit a wide range of audiences.\u00a0 Supervisory Responsibilities: Supervise additional enrollment operations roles Monitor and coordinate workflow and work assignments Delegate and distribute tasks Approve leave requests and timesheets Recommend professional training Evaluate performance, and provide feedback on a consistent basis and in a timely manner Duties/Responsibilities: \u00a0 Data Integrity, Analytics & Reporting\u00a0 Establish and maintain high standards of data accuracy, consistency, and compliance across all admissions systems Develop and manage queries, reports, and dashboards to support recruitment strategy and leadership decision-making Analyze trends in applications, yields, demographics, funnel movement, and territory performance to make recommendations for future admissions cycles\u00a0 Collaborate with Enrollment leadership to support census reporting, funnel reporting, predictive analytics and forecasting Lead the development of an annual analysis of the incoming class profile report to drive strategic planning for future cycles\u00a0 Create and maintain comprehensive process and system documentation Collaborate with the Registrar\u2018s Office, Institutional Research and Information Technology to ensure data alignment and reporting consistency across systems Conduct research on enrollment related topics as requested\u00a0 Systems Administrator\u00a0 Manage and/or track all technologies and 3rd party vendor platforms utilized by Enrollment, including but not limited to Slate, Common App, and CAS systems Provide project management of new implementations and upgrades and assessments of technology or data gaps within Enrollment systems\u00a0 Maintain a calendar of annual operations to guide recruitment and enrollment planning Serve as the primary Slate administrator for Undergraduate Admissions and Graduate and Professional Studies Admissions, Rome City Institute, Study Abroad, Dual Enrollment, and Graduate Advising Oversee the configuration, optimization, and documentation of Slate forms, workflows, queries, rules, and portals\u00a0 Manage Slate user roles, permissions, governance standards Evaluate Slate releases and new functionality; recommend, prioritize and implement system enhancements Act as the primary liaison with Slate support and external vendors for each platform for issue resolution and system improvements Recruitment Support\u00a0 Equip admission counselors with Slate tools for territory management, travel planning, communications, and applicant review Support application reading processes, decision release workflows, and deposit management\u00a0 Cross-Campus Collaboration Ensure close collaboration between Admission offices and campus stakeholders (Student Financial Services, Registrar, Information Technology, Academic Affairs, etc.) Supports partnerships with vendors on integrations, data imports/exports, and system updating and troubleshooting\u00a0 Training \u00a0Provide training on all enrollment technologies and platforms \u00a0 \u00a0Provide onboarding and ongoing Slate training for admission staff and other campus users of Slate\u00a0 \u00a0Promote best practices and user adoption to ensure effective and consistent use of Slate and all other technologies and platforms, as needed\u00a0 Other duties as assigned\u00a0 Preform additional responsibilities as assigned in support of Enrollment Management and institutional priorities\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0Skills and Abilities: \u00a0 Expertise with data structures and analytical tools. Ability to think creatively and analytically. Capacity to prioritize and manage multiple responsibilities and projects concurrenty. Ability to work both independently, with little direct supervision and collaboratively, as a member of a team. A customer-friendly and positive attitude, especially while working under pressure. Cultivate and manage key relationships. Maintain confidential information. Strong leadership skills Supervisory or management experience preferred \u00a0 Education, Certificates, Licenses, and Experience:\u00a0 Bachelor\u2019s degree in Technology -related field or equivalent relevant experience Experience with CRM systems (Slate by Technolutions \u2019 Slate experience is required) High degree of comfort with technology and data management/manipulation Knowledge of third-party application platforms (e.g. Common App, CAS systems) Familiarity with HTML, Liquid Markup, and/or SQL. Relevant technology experience that demonstrates a working knowledge of systems, and data analysis Experience in web design, whether it be building, implementation, or maintenance. \u00a0 Physical Requirements: Must be able to lift and carry equipment and supplies weighing up to 20 pounds. Must be able to bend, stoop, and reach. Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines. Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and by phone. \u00a0 \u00a0 Important Note \u00a0 This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 To Apply Please submit a resume, cover letter, and list of references with the JU Application.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201196538014_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Assistant Coach, Women's Soccer (1st Assistant)", "description": "Posted: 2026-05-27\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION\u00a0 Job Title: Assistant Coach- Women\u2019s Soccer (1st Assistant) Department: Athletics Position Reports to (Position Title): Head Coach- Women\u2019s Soccer Effective Date: July 1st, 2026 \u00a0 Position Class (Exempt or Non-Exempt): Exempt Position Type (Full Time or Part Time): Full Time Is this a Primary or Additional Position: Primary \u00a0 Job Description Primary responsibilities are to assist the Head Coach in all aspects of Division I program including, but not limited to, teaching student athletes how to perform soccer, coordinating team travel arrangements, game day personnel management, and other duties as assigned by the Head Coach or Athletic Administration. This position will also assist the Head Coach in organization, administration, and promotion of the program. Approximately 50% of the Assistant Coach\u2019s responsibility is dedicated to the teaching and instruction of Soccer through on-field (or on-court) training and classroom training through use of video and other teaching techniques. Approximately 50% of the Assistant Coach\u2019s responsibilities are other administrative duties. Candidates must be committed to the academic and athletic success of the student-athletes.\u00a0 Supervisory Responsibilities Graduate Assistants and/or Interns Duties/Responsibilities Assisting with any or all of the following duties as assigned by Head Coach:\u00a0 TEACHING/INSTRUCTING STUDENT-ATHLETES HOW TO DEVELOP AND PERFORM IN THE SPORT OF SOCCER \u2013 Responsible for:\u00a0 \u00b7 Instructing players in the rules, regulations, equipment, and techniques of the sport.\u00a0 \u00b7 Organizing and directing individual and small group practice activities/exercises as directed by the head coach\u00a0 \u00b7 Assess player\u2019s skills, monitors players during competition and practice, and keeps the head coach informed of the athletic performance of students\u00a0 \u00a0 SCHEDULING\u2013 Responsible for:\u00a0 \u00b7 Assisting with scheduling of all competition\u00a0 FINANCIAL AID\u2013 Responsible for:\u00a0 \u00b7 Understanding NCAA regulations\u00a0 \u00b7 Initiating process for initial and renewal grants\u00a0 \u00b7 Consistently updating team rosters\u00a0 \u00b7 Meeting athletic grant-in-aid budget\u00a0 \u00a0 BUDGETS\u2013 Responsible for:\u00a0 \u00b7 Assisting in annual budget preparation\u00a0 \u00b7 Staying within amount budgeted for fiscal year\u00a0 \u00b7 Having all expenditures pre-approved through appropriate channels\u00a0 \u00a0 TRAVEL\u2013 Responsible for:\u00a0 \u00b7 Initiating process for all travel arrangements and submitting reports within 48 hours of return \u00a0 EQUIPMENT/APPAREL\u2013 Responsible for:\u00a0 \u00b7 Pre- and Post-season inventory\u00a0 \u00b7 Care and maintenance of all equipment/apparel and facilities\u00a0 \u00b7 Initiating process to order equipment/apparel\u00a0 \u00a0 ACADEMICS\u2013 Responsible for:\u00a0 \u00b7 Supporting all Department of Athletics policies on classroom attendance, study hall, progress reports and enforcing disciplinary actions\u00a0 \u00b7 Working with teams to maintain and increase their APR\u00a0 \u00a0 FUNDRAISING\u2013 Responsible for:\u00a0 \u00b7 Getting prior approval from the Development office prior to initiating a fund raising activity\u00a0 \u00b7 Devising new methods of fund raising\u00a0 \u00b7 Being available for Departmental fund raising activities\u00a0 \u00b7 Following guidelines established by Department, University, and the NCAA for fund raising activities\u00a0 \u00a0 PAPERWORK \u2013 Responsible for:\u00a0 \u00b7 Completing all paperwork by established athletic department and NCAA deadlines\u00a0 \u00a0 MEETINGS \u2013 Responsible for:\u00a0 \u00b7 Attending and contributing to all Department of Athletics meetings and requested functions \u00a0 CAMPS - Responsible for:\u00a0 \u00b7 Following guidelines established by Department, University, and the NCAA for camp procedures and operations\u00a0 RECRUITING - Responsible for:\u00a0 \u00b7 Compliance with NCAA recruiting rules and completing associated paperwork in a timely manner \u00b7 Arranging financially responsible recruiting trips\u00a0 \u00b7 Initiating arrangements for all official visits\u00a0 \u00b7 Recruiting student who will be an asset to the University and Department of Athletics and graduate in a timely manner \u00a0 Required Skills/Abilities \u00b7 Knowledge of NCAA Rules and Regulations \u00b7\u00a0Mastery of sport coached \u00b7 Ability to lead, guide and direct graduate assistants, interns and student-athletes\u00a0 \u00b7 Willingness to form relationships with constituents and help fundraise Education, Certificates, Licenses, and Experience 1. Minimum Education Requirement:\u00a0 \u00b7\u00a0Bachelor\u2019s degree from accredited college or university, master\u2019s degree preferred \u00a02. Minimum Work Experience:\u00a0 \u00b7 Two years collegiate coaching experience at NCAA Division I level preferred\u00a0 3. Preferred Qualifications:\u00a0 \u00b7 Experience with NCAA Division I Rules and Regulations\u00a0 \u00b7 Proven recruiting abilities\u00a0 \u00b7 Demonstrated leadership skills Physical Requirements \u00b7Must be able to physically perform essential job duties or have special accommodations arranged in advance Work Conditions \u00b7 Required to work atypical hours including nights, weekends, potential holidays \u00b7 May be required to practice in heat, cold, inclement weather Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. To Apply Interested applicants are asked to submit a resume with this application.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201169687336_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "\ud83c\udf3fGuest Artist, LBSCOAS - Application by invitation only.", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-19\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION\u00a0 Job Title: Guest Artist, LBSCOAS Department: Linda Berry Stein College of Fine Arts & Sciences \u00a0 \u00a0 Position Reports to: Dean, LNSCOAS Position Class: Exempt (as applicable) \u00a0 Job Summary - Only individuals invited by the LBS College of Arts and Sciences are eligible to apply. The Guest Artist is a distinguished practitioner invited to contribute specialized artistic/scholastic expertise to the University community. This position enhances the academic experience of students through performances, workshops, masterclasses, lectures, critiques, or short-term instructional engagements. The Guest Artist collaborates with faculty and students to support creative, scholarly, and professional development aligned with the mission of the institution. Duties/Responsibilities Present public performances, exhibitions, readings, lectures, screenings, or demonstrations as scheduled. Conduct masterclasses, workshops, lectures, or direction/rehearsals for students. Provide individual or group critiques and mentorship to students. Collaborate with faculty on curriculum-related activities and special projects. Participate in panel discussions, community outreach, or campus engagement events as requested. Attend rehearsals or preparatory meetings as appropriate. Uphold University policies, procedures, and community standards during the engagement period. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree in a relevant discipline or equivalent professional experience. Recognized professional achievement in the artistic field. Demonstrated experience in performance, exhibition, or professional artistic practice. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree or terminal degree (MFA, DMA, PhD, or equivalent) in the relevant discipline. Prior experience teaching or working with university students. Regional, national, or international recognition in the field. Experience engaging diverse audiences and academic communities. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Expertise in a specific discipline (e.g., instrumental/vocal performance, theatre, dance, visual arts, film, creative writing). Ability to engage, inspire, and mentor students. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Professionalism and collaborative approach within an academic environment. Terms of Appointment Appointment is temporary and limited to the duration of the engagement. Compensation will be determined based on scope of services, credentials, and budget approval. Housing, travel, and other expenses may be provided in accordance with University policy and contractual agreement. Work Environment The position may require rehearsal, performance, studio, classroom, or gallery environments. Evening or weekend commitments may be required depending on event scheduling. Only individuals invited by the LBS College of Arts and Sciences are eligible to apply.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9200557661434_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "\ud83c\udf3fCampus Safety & Security Officer", "description": "Posted: 2024-05-16\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nSummary Position Title Campus Safety and Security Officer Department Campus Safety and Security Status Full Time/Non-Exempt Position Summary Patrols University grounds and buildings in order to provide a visible presence to deter crime; respond to all emergencies and routine calls for services in a timely manner and coordinate the police, fire and or medical response to same; Provide general safety information through the daily interaction with the University. Monitor campus special events and parking areas. Dispatch calls and answer Campus Security telephones, assist members of the community who may have questions. Take photo ID pictures and issue identification cards. Issue parking permits and enforce traffic and parking regulations. Position requires minor physical exertion including the consistent need to push, pull, carry, and lift up to 25 pounds on a regular basis and the ability to stand and/or walk for lengthy periods of time without rest or assistance. The Campus Security Officer works within a 24 hour/7 day operation and due to the nature of the position, the Campus Security Officer should expect to work a fluctuating work schedule including holidays, nights and weekends.\u00a0 Essential Job Duties Serve as a visible and proactive University representative within a 24/7 department charged with providing a secure environment for the University students, affiliates, quests and visitors. Conduct patrols via foot and mountain style bikes to respond to emergencies, provide services and access functions as appropriate, personal escort services. Provide safety awareness through daily contact with the University community and visitors by providing general safety information, directions, parking information. Identify actual or potential safety hazards or conditions and coordinate a resolution with the appropriate department or area. Provide assistance to University personnel in matters involving potential violations to University policy wherein conduct or behavioral expectations are disruptive to the mission of the University. Respond to all emergencies to coordinate law enforcement, medical and/or fire services response to the incident, and to provide a proactive role after the emergency situation has concluded. Make appropriate notifications on campus emergencies as directed. Prepare incident reports and related written communication and maintain activity logs as appropriate. Answer telephones. Dispatch calls via two-way radio. Work special events to provide traffic, parking, and crowd control as needed. Assist the parking program by monitoring parking areas, issuing citations and maintaining access to fire lanes, handicap spaces, and the roadways owned and or controlled by the University. Performs other related duties as assigned by the Director of Campus Security, Coordinator, or assigned Shift Supervisor.\u00a0 Education and Experience: H.S. Diploma or GED required. A current and valid State of Florida Class D Security Officer License is required. Ability to be creative in developing solutions to complex problems and to multi-task in a fast-paced environment. Ability to provide instruction on personal safety and security issues. Must have a valid driver's license. Must be able to pass a comprehensive background check. Associate Degree is preferred or commensurate experience in the military, law enforcement. or security, preferably on a college campus. Excellent communication skills with a wide variety of people is required. Some typing is required, ability to type 15 wpm. Use of word processing, spreadsheets, database, and email programs required. Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. To Apply Interested candidates should submit a copy of their resume, cover letter, and list of references with this application.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201224854299_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Career Advisor", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJob Title:\u00a0 Career Advisor Department:\u00a0 Career Design & Exploration Position Reports to:\u00a0 Associate Director, Career Design & Exploration Effective Date:\u00a0 9/4/2026 Position Class/Type: Exempt, Full-Time Job Summary The Career Advisor plays a critical role in expanding student access to career services and delivering high-quality career readiness programming. This position provides direct student support through individual coaching, group programming, and event execution, while supporting the day-to-day operations of the Career Design & Exploration office. The Career Advisor focuses on high-volume student engagement, career education delivery, and logistical execution of career programs and events. This role collaborates closely with the Associate Director and Director to ensure students have timely, equitable access to career resources, experiences, and opportunities that support their academic and professional success. Supervisory Responsibilities: This role supervises undergraduate student staff. Duties/Responsibilities: Individual Student Support (50%) Provide one-on-one career counseling and coaching, including: Resume and cover letter reviews. Interview preparation and mock interviews. Internship and job search strategies. Networking and professional branding (LinkedIn, Handshake, personal statements, etc.). Salary negotiation and offer evaluation guidance. Serve as a primary point of access for students seeking career services, ensuring timely support and appropriate referrals. Support students in navigating career platforms and\u00a0tools, including Handshake and other career technologies. Assist with triaging career-related inquiries from students, alumni, and campus partners. Career Programming & Workshop Delivery (20%) Plan, coordinate, and deliver career readiness workshops and programs focused on: Career exploration Resume and interview preparation Job and internship search strategies Workplace professionalism and expectations Execute logistics for career-related programming, including room scheduling, registration, materials, and attendance tracking. Collaborate with campus partners to\u00a0support co-sponsored career programs and increase student participation. Assist with the assessment of career programs to ensure alignment with student needs and institutional goals. Career Intern Supervision (15%) Supervise Career Interns, providing training, mentorship, and professional development opportunities to support career programming and daily operations. Berwick Career Closet Oversight Marketing Initiatives Operations and Events Coordinate Career Intern assignments, projects, and\u00a0daily responsibilities to\u00a0align with departmental priorities and career services initiatives. Foster a supportive and professional team environment by conducting regular 1:1s, providing performance feedback, evaluating student progress, and encouraging the development of career competencies. Event Coordination & Execution (10%) Support the planning and execution of major career-related events, including: Professional development sessions and workshops On-campus recruitment activities Career fairs and networking events Coordinate event logistics, including employer communication, student registration, and on-site support. Track participation and support post-event follow-up activities. Operational Support (5%) Provide operational support for the day-to-day functions of the Career Design & Exploration office, ensuring smooth delivery of student-facing services. Assist with the coordination and execution of office initiatives, projects, and special events as assigned. Serve as a point of contact for routine inquiries, escalating complex issues to the Associate Director or Director as appropriate. Required Skills/Abilities: Strong interpersonal skills and a student-centered approach, with the ability to engage effectively with diverse populations. Comfort with frequent student interaction in a high-volume, service-oriented environment. Ability to\u00a0collaborate effectively with professional staff, faculty, student employees, and campus partners. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite, Microsoft Outlook, and database or CRM systems. Ability to\u00a0manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment while maintaining high levels of accuracy and service quality. Demonstrated ability to maintain confidentiality and discretion when handling sensitive information. Education, Certificates, Licenses, and Experience: Bachelor\u2019s degree required Master\u2019s degree in higher education/student affairs or related field from a regionally accredited college or university preferred; A minimum of six months to two years of experience, on a college or university campus Physical Requirements: Must be able to lift and carry equipment and supplies weighing up to 20 pounds. Must be able to bend, stoop, and reach. Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines. Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and by phone. Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. Acknowledgment Submission of my application acknowledges receipt and understanding of this job description. I verify that I am capable of and willing to fulfill all essential functions of this position. I am willing to be flexible and willing to do various jobs that are not listed, as the need arises.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201226537586_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Assistant Director Graduate Prof Studies", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-14\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION Job Title: Assistant Director, Graduate and Professional Studies Admission- Recruiter Department: Enrollment Management \u2013 Graduate Admissions Position Reports to (Position Title): \u00a0Associate Director , Graduate Recruitment Position Class: Exempt Position Type: Full Time/ Primary Position Job Summary The Assistant Director of Graduate and Professions Studies Admissions is responsible for \u00a0recruiting, matriculation, academic advising and program management. The Assistant Director will proactively seek out prospective candidates and represent the University at graduate recruitment fairs and events. A successful candidate will have a proven track record of specialized sales, preferably in the professional recruitment of higher education sectors. Looking for self-starting, motivated, relationship-driven, strong communicator who works well independently and with a team Supervisory Responsibilities: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 None Duties/Responsibilities: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Proactively creates an outbound recruitment strategy to identify and develop new graduate student candidates. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Provides consultative services to prospective students regarding all details of the programs including application, matriculation, course overviews, program requirements, academic policies and procedures. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Schedules/hosts official application interviews with each candidate; makes recommendations as part of admissions selection committee. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Represents Jacksonville University at local and global recruitment fairs. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Works collaboratively with the Director of Graduate Enrollment Management to address recruitment issues and opportunities while developing comprehensive strategies to achieve annual target enrollment goals. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Refines and hosts information sessions for prospects and yield events for admitted applicants. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Supports the development and utilization of recruiting management system; especially to build a strong communication flow for prospective and matriculated students. Develops and maintains cooperative relationships with other schools and universities. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Provides expertise on recruitment strategies to marketing team \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Perform other relevant duties as assigned Required Skills/Abilities: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Specialized and relationship-based sales and/or recruiting experience with proven track record of achieving goals. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Able to develop, plan and achieve short and long-range goals. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Strong analytical and problem-solving skills; ability to evaluate data, assess alternatives and make appropriate decisions/recommendations. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Strong interpersonal and communication skills, including oral, written; especially for presentations. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Demonstrates tact and diplomacy, maintaining a high level of confidentiality. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Strong organizational, time management and project-management skills. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Motivated to work independently but able to thrive and contribute in a team-oriented environment \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Computer proficiency in MS Office Suite, Google and other basic software Education, Certificates, Licenses, and Experience: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Master\u2019s degree or equivalent combination of education and experience \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Experience working in a graduate academic setting, in a business school, with students who are professional working adults, and/or with international students is preferred. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Experience with higher education recruitment and admission preferred Physical Requirements: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Must be able to lift and carry equipment and supplies weighing up to 20 pounds. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Must be able to bend, stoop, and reach. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0 Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and by phone Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. To Apply Interested candidates are asked to submit a resume and cover letter with a JU application.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201228374579_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Simulationist", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION\u00a0 Job Title: Simulationist\u00a0 Department: Keigwin School of Nursing and\u00a0 Brooks Rehabilitation College of Healthcare Sciences Position Reports to (Position Title): Director of Simulation and Department Chair of Simulation Position Class (Exempt or Non-Exempt): Exempt Position Type (Full Time or Part Time): Full Time Is this a Primary or Additional Position: Primary \u00a0 Job Summary Facilitate the daily operations of the Keigwin School of Nursing (KSON) Simulation Training and Applied Research (STAR) Center and Clinical Skills Lab under the direction of the Simulation Director and Department Chair. The Simulation Center and Clinical Skills Lab are environments that support critical thinking and experiential learning experiences for KSON students, Brooks Rehabilitation College of Healthcare Sciences (BRCHS) students, and community partners. The simulationist will participate in the delivery of clinical simulation experiences and the operation of manikin simulators or standardized patients (SPs) to be used effectively in healthcare education and training. Duties/Responsibilities Collaborate with the Director of the Simulation, the Department Chair of Simulation, KSON faculty, BRCHS faculty, and community partners to maximize the utilization of clinical learning in simulation centers Collaborate and implement current evidence-based practice in simulation learning set by the International Nursing Association for Clinical Simulation and Learning (INACSL) Organize and execute the set-up and breakdown of equipment, supplies, and materials for scheduled courses and simulations in the lab and\u00a0classrooms. This includes standardized patient and simulators moulage. Operate simulation software and audiovisual equipment Collect and analyze lab survey responses for assigned courses to determine the effectiveness of simulation on student learning, critical thinking, and clinical decision- making. Discuss the findings with the Simulation Director to\u00a0identify potential improvements. Assist in the operation of manikin simulators and Standardized Patients (SPs) to facilitate their use in healthcare education and training Develop and create ways to enhance learning in the lab, such as facilitating lunch and learns, and other coordinated activities Provide for the general cleanliness and security of the laboratory. Appropriate disposal of hazardous materials for OSHA standards. Collaborate with the Simulation Director to engage faculty & community partners in developing, implementing, and evaluating courses, simulation scenarios, simulation tools, and other educational initiatives to promote and measure student learning outcomes Communicate and collaborate in a positive, professional manner with the Director of the Simulation, Department Chair of Simulation, faculty, simulationists, and IT operation specialists Collaborate with Simulation Operations and IT specialists to maintain, troubleshoot, and resolve issues related to the operation and maintenance of simulation equipment. Participate in grant and contractual-related activities as designated by the Director of Simulation Remain current with developments in the field of simulation technology and learning theory. Maintain records of experiential learning activities in an electronic database Participate in professional development and attend professional meetings and conferences Attend regularly scheduled JU KSON meetings and activities as appropriate Participate in simulation meetings for the STAR Center and Skills Lab Participate in KSON organization committee(s) Serve as a mentor and role model for students in the lab Perform other related duties as assigned. Required Skills/Abilities Excellent communication skills (both verbal and written) Technologically inclined and proficient in Microsoft applications Familiar with the healthcare environment and operations, proficient in medical terminology, and well-versed in clinical practices.\u202f Excellent interpersonal and organizational skills Innovative Best Practice simulation implementation and use of simulation technology. Ability to\u00a0work collaboratively with the simulation team, Jacksonville University faculty and staff, and interdisciplinary community partners. May travel between campus buildings or off-campus. Able to work with self-initiative and autonomy. Simulation experience preferred. Education, Certificates, Licenses, and Experience:\u00a0 A bachelor's degree from an accredited institution is required. A degree in nursing or other healthcare related field preferred. Previous simulation experience.\u00a0 Certified Healthcare Simulation Educator or Operator preferred or a desire to work towards it. Physical Recquirements Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines. Near vision sufficient to read written communications and computer display screens. Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and by phone. No limitations on physical lifting ability of simulation manikins and equipment up to 80 lbs. with assistance.\u00a0 No Latex Allergy.\u00a0 Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. \u00a0 To Apply Interested applicants are asked to submit a resume along with a JU application.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201231519524_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "KSON Nursing Programs Coordinator", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION\u00a0 Job Title:\u00a0 \u00a0KSON Nursing Programs Coordinator & Social Media Content Creator\u00a0 Department:\u00a0 Keigwin School of Nursing Position Reports to (Position Title):\u00a0 Director of Entry Level Programs and Associate Dean of Nursing Position Class (Exempt or Non-Exempt): Exempt Position Type (Full Time or Part Time): Full Time\u00a0 \u00a0 Job Summary This position assists the Entry and Advanced Level-Directors of the Keigwin School of Nursing. It requires the incumbent to assume responsibility for a variety of activities related to the operationalizing the various nursing programs. This position works in collaboration with nursing faculty and other administrative personnel in the Keigwin School of Nursing. Supervisor Responsibilities Student workers\u00a0 Duties/Responsibilities Administrative Support and Communications Provides administrative support to program directors Serves as the primary point of contact for visitors to the KSON building and for communication with Nursing Program Directors. Communicates building-related information, submits work orders, and ensures compliance with safety protocols. Attends committee meetings within KSON as assigned by Program Directors Scheduling and Operational Management Maintains the master schedule for all KSON programs, including faculty load assignments, adjunct and overload scheduling, and classroom coordination Manages daily operational activities for the KSON, including updates to the website, distribution of student announcements, and oversight of social media platforms. Manages and schedules conference rooms within the BRCHS building. Oversees the scheduling, task assignment, and supervision of student workers in alignment with the goals of KSON leadership. Assists with the creation, management, and maintenance of KSON policies and procedures in collaboration with Directors and the Associate Dean. Student Engagement and Events Assists in planning and implementing student activities and KSON events in collaboration with KSON leadership and faculty Develops, organizes, and maintains nursing student engagement projects. Serves as a liaison for nursing student tours and the entry-level nursing program ambassador program. Coordinates with Nursing Program Directors to assess and support student needs. Marketing and Social Media Collaborates with the Department Chair of Online, Cohorts, and Marketing to manage KSON\u2019s social media presence Creates, posts, and advertises events on social media platforms in alignment with the KSON mission and policies. Monitors social media accounts and responds to comments in a professional and timely manner. Data and Reporting Assists in the aggregation of program data and preparation of reports.\u00a0 Other Performs other duties as assigned to support the mission and operations of the Keigwin School of Nursing. Required Skills/Abilities Excellent communication skills (both veral and written) Understanding of and commitment to the use of technology Proficiency in social media applications, especially Facebook and Twitter Proficiency in Microsoft Office, especially Microsoft Word and Excel Strong organizational skills Event planning Customer-focused approach Education, Experience, Licenses & Certifications Bachelor\u2019s degree Master's Degree (preferred) Knowledge of nursing profession and educational requirements, experience in advising preferred Experience working in a diverse environment Preferred: experience working in organization systems management and/or leadership Preferred: experience working in a university environment. Physical Requirements Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines Near vision sufficient to read written communications and computer display screens Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and by phone No limitations on physical lifting ability \u00a0 Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs.\u00a0 To Apply Interested applicants are asked to submit a resume, cover letter, list of references with a JU application.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201231562923_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Asst Director Admissions Events & Engagement", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJob Title: Assistant Director, Admissions Events and Engagement \u00a0 Department: Enrollment Management\u00a0 Position Reports to: Associate Director of Events and Management Position Class/Position Type: Exempt, Full-Time Primary or Additional Position: Primary Job Summary The Assistant Director of Admissions Events & Engagement maintains responsibility for activities related to admissions events and the campus visit experience. The person in this position will support events in Undergraduate Admission, Graduate and Professional Studies Admission, and the College of Law departments. They will perform duties that assure a quality campus event experience, develop and align the campus event experience with the University brand and enrollment goals including training and supervision of student ambassadors. This position reports to the Associate Director of Admission Events and Engagement. Supervisory Responsibilities Student Ambassadors, shared responsibility with Associate Director \u00a0 Duties/Responsibilities Design, plan, implement and manage customized events, considering past experiences and data-driven reports Consult with the Directors of Undergraduate and Graduate Admissions in planning event logistics and execution, working primarily with the leadership team and with campus partners involved in event setup and event participation Create event setup memos, meet with facilities, catering, security and custodians as well as Information Technology, as necessary Work closely with the Enrollment Marketing on both in-person and virtual events in the CRM system Supports in River House event management inclusive of approval, SA scheduling, floor plans, facility upkeep, AV and more. Ensure selection and booking of appropriate spaces and resources for each event and order other equipment as needed Coordinate staff roles and train all student workers/ambassadors and/or volunteers Conduct event meetings and orchestrate physical set-ups and breakdowns of each event Participate in event evaluations and gather feedback from various departments, campus partners and staff to make improvements to future events Work with the Associate Director of Admissions Events and Engagement on event support, which includes scheduling campus tours and tour guides. Assists at off-campus recruitment events, if required Perform other duties and projects as assigned. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice \u00a0 Required Skills/Abilities Flexibility and adaptability Collaborative, supportive leader and teammate Excellent organization and project management skills Excellent communication and customer service skills Ability to\u00a0use discretionary judgment Demonstrated tech savviness and ability to learn and\u00a0operate different systems Manage, train, develop, and support a team of Student Ambassadors A person of character, drive and integrity who will always represent the University in a professional manner. Ability to\u00a0meet appropriate situations with reasonable, creative responses to\u00a0achieve the goals and objectives of the recruitment effort. Dedicated to the mission of Jacksonville University regarding the growth of its student population. \u00a0 Education, Certificates, Licenses, and Experience Bachelor\u2019s degree required. Master\u2019s degree and admissions related work and/or related experience in a college environment are highly desirable. Commitment to customer service, both internal and external to the department. Experience using a CRM to develop and implement events, multi-level communication campaigns and reports. SLATE experience preferred. Understanding of college admissions Strong interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills to\u00a0effectively communicate with students, co-workers, and the general public. Ability to\u00a0speak effectively before groups of students, parents and community members Demonstrated time management experience Demonstrated organizational skills and attention to detail. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple tasks. Ability to\u00a0exercise sound judgment in a fast-paced work environment. Sensitivity toward people of diverse social, cultural and ethnic backgrounds. Willing to work as part of a team and understand the importance of teamwork Physical Requirements:\u00a0 Must be able to lift and carry equipment and supplies weighing up to 20 pounds. Must be able to bend, stoop, and reach. Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines. Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and by phone Important Note\u00a0 This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. \u00a0 To Apply Interest applicants are asked to submit a resume and cover letter with a JU application.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201231532840_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Asst. Dir., UG Admissions Strategic Recruitment", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJob Title: Assistant Director, UG Admissions-Strategic Recruitment \u00a0 Department: Enrollment Management-Undergraduate Admissions\u00a0 Position Reports to: Director, Undergraduate Recruitment\u00a0 Position Class: Exempt Position Type: Full Time Primary or Additional Position: Primary Job Summary: \u00a0 The Assistant Director of Strategic Recruitment will serve as part of the team continuing to recruit and enroll prospective students into Jacksonville University. The position will support new operational initiatives to support strategic functions of student recruitment. The position will continue to build professional relationships with prospective students through multiple mediums while also navigating national trends, and data review. The position will evaluate applications, support documentation, and advise students, families, and counselors in finding the right fit university. \u00a0 Supervisory Responsibilities:\u00a0 Support and oversee travel and territory breakdown for admission staff and support data for recruitment strategies and initiatives. \u00a0 Duties and Responsibilities:\u00a0 Manage assigned recruitment territory, including reviewing applications, maintaining accurate territory data and records, and communicating with prospective students, applicants, families, school counselors, consultants, and recruitment partners throughout the admissions process. Drive student recruitment and take responsibility supporting implementation of efficient reports, queries, and voyagers built for undergraduate admission counselors. Assist Associate Director of Recruitment with travel planning and reporting initiatives. Develop resources for recruiters to use in their personal recruitment strategy. Develop projects/strategies that leverage out of state partnerships to achieve enrollment goals. Cultivate and explore new relationships that can drive and improve our recruitment plan. This includes representing the University to local schools, community partners, or educational consultants.\u00a0 Collaborates with internal university departments to research, collate, and share with colleagues, information, and data relevant to the recruitment landscape.\u00a0 Ensure the maintenance of records and reporting in relation to the monitoring of student recruitment.\u00a0 Contribute with onboarding new admissions counselors primarily focused on procedures, travel planning, and report building. Performs other duties as assigned. \u00a0 Required Skills/Abilities: Ability to\u00a0think critically and independently solve problems. Clear, correct, and effective communication skills. Person of character, drive and integrity who will always represent the University in a professional manner. Ability to\u00a0meet appropriate situations with reasonable, creative responses to\u00a0achieve the goals and objectives of the recruitment effort. Dedicated to the mission of Jacksonville University about the growth of its student population. \u00a0 Education, Certificates, Licenses, and Experience: Bachelor\u2019s degree in any field Strong understanding of the admissions cycle, application review process, student recruitment, and key industry metrics Experience developing and implementing strategic initiatives and planning recruitment travel. Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite, Google, and other basic technology.\u00a0 Experience with Technolutions Slate preferred \u00a0 Physical Requirements: Must be able to lift and carry equipment and supplies weighing up to 20 pounds. Must be able to bend, stoop, and reach. Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines. Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and by phone. Ability to operate a multi-passenger golf cart \u00a0 Important Note\u00a0 This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. \u00a0 \u00a0 To Apply Interested applicants are asked to submit a resume and cover letter with a JU application.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201233357602_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Assistant Director, UG Admissions - Recruitment Management", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJob Title:\u00a0 Assistant Director, UG Admissions-Recruitment Engagement \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Department:\u00a0 Enrollment Management-Undergraduate Admissions Position Reports to:\u00a0 Director, Undergraduate Recruitment Position Class/Position Type: Exempt, Full-Time \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Job Summary:\u00a0 The Assistant Director of Recruitment Engagement will serve as a key member of the team responsible for recruiting and enrolling prospective students at Jacksonville University. This position will oversee the operational and strategic functions of recruited student engagement, including the effective use of vendors and specialty scholarship programs. The Assistant Director will develop and maintain professional relationships with prospective students through multiple communication channels and engagement opportunities, leveraging internal and external partnerships, vendor resources, and other tools designed to support effective relationship management. Additionally, the position will evaluate applications and supporting documentation, counsel prospective students throughout the recruitment and enrollment process, and provide recommendations to University leadership regarding recruitment strategies and initiatives. \u00a0 \u00a0Supervisory Responsibilities:\u00a0 None \u00a0 \u00a0Duties and Responsibilities:\u00a0 Integrate vendor partnerships to enhance recruitment and student engagement throughout the admissions cycle. Use current undergraduate vendors to enhance our overall resources for students. Analyze current and historical enrollment trends in assigned territory to develop a strategy that serves the University\u2019s enrollment goals. This position will create and implement an outline of goals to help build upon student engagement to promote Jacksonville University. Develop projects/strategies that leverage partnerships to achieve enrollment goals. Cultivate and explore new relationships that can drive and improve our recruitment plan. This includes representing the University to schools, community partners, or educational consultants. Communicate with applicants, parents, advisors, consultants and recruiting partners to facilitate the admissions process. Collaborates with internal university departments to research, collate, and share with colleagues, information, and data relevant to support prospective student scholarships. Ensure the maintenance of records and reporting in relation to the monitoring of student recruitment.\u00a0 Contribute with onboarding new admissions counselors. Performs other duties as assigned. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0Required Skills/Abilities: Experience working with diverse student populations in advising and/or recruitment roles. Strong interpersonal and organizational skills. Ability to\u00a0work well in a team environment. Excellent written and oral communication skills with a high level of tact and follow- through. Excellent analytical skills, and problem-solving skills. Ability to\u00a0establish and maintain effective and collaborative relationships. Demonstrated ability to maintain accurate and detailed records, and experience with preparing and submitting reports for accountability purposes. A person of character, drive and integrity who will always represent the University in a professional manner. Ability to\u00a0meet appropriate situations with reasonable, creative responses to\u00a0achieve the goals and objectives of the recruitment effort. Dedicated to the mission of Jacksonville University regarding the growth of its student population. \u00a0 Education, Certificates, Licenses, and Experience: Bachelor\u2019s Degree in any field. Strong understanding of the admissions cycle, application review process, student recruitment, and key industry metrics. Experience developing and implementing strategic initiatives and planning recruitment travel. Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite, Google, and other basic technology. Experience with Technolutions Slate preferred \u00a0 \u00a0Physical Requirements: Must be able to lift and carry equipment and supplies weighing up to 20 pounds. Must be able to bend, stoop, and reach. Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines. Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and by phone. Ability to operate a multi-passenger golf cart \u00a0 Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. \u00a0 \u00a0 To Apply Interested applicants are asked to submit a resume and cover letter with a JU application.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201235151075_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Asso. Dir. UG Admis Student Engage Recruitmen", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJob Title: Associate Director, UG Admissions-Student Engagement and Recruitment Department: Enrollment Management-Undergraduate Admissions\u00a0 Position Reports to (Position Title): Director, Undergraduate Recruitment\u00a0 Position Class/Position Type: Exempt, Full-Time Primary or Additional Position: Primary \u00a0 Job Summary The Associate Director of UG Admissions \u2013 Student Engagement & Recruitment is responsible for leading undergraduate student recruitment and enrollment efforts for Jacksonville University in Florida and throughout the Southeast, with a particular focus on local recruitment and community engagement. The Associate Director will lead the development and implementation of recruitment and student engagement initiatives, build and maintain professional relationships with prospective students and key internal and external partners, and manage recruitment efforts across multiple mediums and venues, including in-person events, virtual platforms, social media, and other relationship-management tools. The Associate Director will manage and support a team of admissions counselors, provide guidance throughout the recruitment and enrollment process, and collaborate with university partners to strengthen internal recruitment and engagement efforts. The position will also evaluate applications and supporting documentation, advise prospective students through the admissions and enrollment process, and identify opportunities to improve conversion and enrollment outcomes. The Associate Director will monitor key recruitment and enrollment metrics, assess progress toward enrollment goals throughout the admissions cycle, and use data and market insights to inform recruitment strategies and priorities. This position will play a key role in strengthening Jacksonville University\u2019s presence in the local and regional markets while supporting broader institutional enrollment objectives and will make recommendations to university leadership regarding recruitment strategy, market opportunities, and initiatives to support enrollment growth. Supervisory Resonsibilities: Interviews, hires and trains new staff. Oversees the daily workflow of the department. Evaluates staff performance and provides timely feedback. Helps to resolve employee issues and disputes. Handles discipline and termination of employees in accordance with university policy. \u00a0 Duties/Responsibilities:\u00a0 Communicate and provide support to prospective students, applicants, parents, advisors, consultants, recruiting partners, and other stakeholders to facilitate the admissions and enrollment process and provide a high level of service. Manage, train, develop, and support a team of admissions counselors, providing guidance and direction to ensure effective recruitment and student engagement practices. Ensure accurate and timely maintenance of recruitment records, data, and reporting related to local and assigned-territory recruitment activities and outcomes. Analyze current and historical enrollment trends in assigned territories, with particular attention to the local Jacksonville market, to develop recruitment strategies that support the University\u2019s enrollment goals. Develop and implement goals, projects, and strategies that strengthen Jacksonville University\u2019s local internal and external relationships and leverage community partnerships to\u00a0support enrollment goals. Make recommendations to the Director of Undergraduate Recruitment and the Vice President of Enrollment Management regarding admissions processes, recruitment initiatives, local market opportunities, and strategies to support enrollment growth. Cultivate and explore new relationships, partnerships, and networks that can enhance local recruitment efforts and increase Jacksonville University\u2019s visibility within the community. Make individual and large- or small-group presentations to\u00a0prospective students, families, school counselors, community partners, and other audiences regarding Jacksonville University and its academic programs. Collaborate with internal University departments to\u00a0research, collect, analyze, and share information and data relevant to the local marketplace, recruitment activities, and enrollment opportunities. Integrate vendor partnerships and utilize current undergraduate recruitment resources to enhance student engagement, recruitment efforts, and the overall resources available to prospective students throughout the admissions cycle. Provide recommendations to\u00a0University leadership regarding local and regional recruitment strategy, emerging market trends, partnership opportunities, and initiatives that may strengthen student recruitment and enrollment. Provide excellent customer service and maintain a student-centered approach in every aspect of the role. Work autonomously, demonstrate initiative and proactive problem-solving, and make ethical and sound decisions in support of University and enrollment objectives. Performs other duties as assigned. \u00a0 Required Skills/Abilities:\u00a0 Flexibility and adaptability Collaborative, supportive leader and teammate Excellent organization and project management skills Excellent communication and customer service skills Demonstrated tech savviness and ability to learn and\u00a0operate different systems. Person of character, drive and integrity who will always represent the University in a professional manner Ability to\u00a0meet appropriate situation with reasonable, creative responses to\u00a0achieve the goals and objectives of the recruitment effort Dedicated to the mission of Jacksonville University regarding the growth of its student population \u00a0 Education, Certificates, Licenses, and Experience:\u00a0 Bachelor\u2019s required, in any field 3+ years working in enrollment management, preferably in undergraduate admissions 1+ years managerial experience Strong understanding of the admissions cycle, application review process, student recruitment, and key industry metrics Experience developing and implementing strategic initiatives and planning recruitment travel Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite, Google, and other basic technology; Experience with Technolutions Slate preferred \u00a0 Physical Requirements: Must be able to lift and carry equipment and supplies weighing up to 20 pounds. Must be able to bend, stoop, and reach. Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines. Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and by phone. \u00a0 Important Note \u00a0 This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. \u00a0 \u00a0 To Apply Interested applicants are asked to submit a resume and cover letter with a JU application.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201235431283_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Office Associate, Social Sciences & Education", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-17\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nPosition Title: Office Associate -\u00a0 School of Social Science & Education, Department of Humanities, and College of Law Department: Linda Berry Stein College of Arts & Sciences Position Reports to: Dean of Linda Berry Stein College of Arts & Sciences Position Type: \u00a0 Full-Time, Exempt Position Summary:\u00a0 This position is responsible for providing administrative support to the School of Social Sciences and Education. The Department of Humanities, and the College of Law. The position is full-time and shared between Social Sciences, Education, Humanities, College of Law, and the stein College of Arts & Sciences. \u00a0Supervisory Responsibilities: The position hires, reviews, supervises, and terminates student workers.\u00a0 Duties/Responsibilities:\u00a0 -Provide administrative support to the Director of Social Sciences & Education, Chair of Humanities, Chair of Education, the College of Law, and the students and faculty within these divisions. -Assist with administrative duties including record keeping, work orders, purchase requests, invoice tracking, PCard purchases, processing mail, maintaining copiers, maintaining buildings (Gooding, Council, and Founders buildings), onboarding adjuncts, hiring and supervising student workers. -Submit key requests, name badge orders, and office supply requests for new faculty. Provide administrative support for new full-time and adjunct faculty. -Manage the organization of events including catering, 25 Live, invitations, tracking attendance, decorations, and other details as needed per event. -Collaborate with Chairs to create and submit Payroll Sheets each semester. -Assist faculty in arranging field trips and professional development travel arrangements. -Foster and maintain a professional and friendly office environment, including assisting students and visitors with directions and with faculty or department contact information, and maintaining organized and clean offices and supply rooms. -Monitor website pages for any needed updates. -Coordinate faculty search campus visits by creating the daily interview schedules and working with the Director of College Operations to ensure hotel, travel, and Dean\u2019s availability -Other duties as assigned by the Dean\u2019s Office Education and Experience: \u00a0 Minimum Education Requirement: High school diploma Minimum Work Experience: -\u00a02+ years in a professional office environment providing administrative support Advanced Microsoft Excel, Word, PowerPoint, Outlook, and Office skills Customer service experience \u00a0Preferred Qualifications:\u00a0 -Superior written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills with a strong dedication to customer service. -Experience working with multiple teams and in a higher education environment. -Demonstrated proactive problem-solving skills and ability to work under stress and time pressures. -Strong organizational, time management, and communication skills. -Ability to set priorities, make timely decisions, and meet deadlines while working on multiple projects. -Possess high standards of ethics, accuracy, and precision. -Ability to think creatively, highly driven, and self-motivated. -Knowledge of basic bookkeeping/accounts payable principles. Physical Requirements: - Must be able to lift and carry equipment and supplies weighing up to 40 lbs. -Must be able to stoop, bend, and reach -Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines -Near vision sufficient to read written communications and computer display screens -Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and by phone Work Conditions -Work is primarily indoors, but requires the employee to be in an outdoor environment when traveling between campus buildings or being off-campus -Standard office hours are 8:30 am to 5:00 pm -Employee will be exposed to frequent noise caused by telephones, operating functions, and office machines Important Note: This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. Acknowledgment: Submission of my application acknowledges receipt and understanding of this job description. I verify that I am capable of and willing to fulfill all essential functions of this position. I am willing to be flexible and willing to do various jobs that are not listed, as the need arises.", "department": ""}}, "rows": {"https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201218545086_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 235, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201218545086_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Coach, Men's Rowing", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Athletics meetings and requested functions\u00a0 CAMPS", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-08-14", "position_start_date": "08/20/2026"}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201216017705_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 235, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201216017705_1&lang=en_US", "job